`parseHeader`:
```
func parseHeader(line string) (int, string, bool) {
    if !strings.HasPrefix(line, "#") {
        return 0, "", false
    }
    level := 0
    for level < len(line) && line[level] == '#' {
        level++
    }
    if level < 1 || level > 7 {
        return 0, "", false
    }
    if level == len(line) {
        return level, "", true
    }
    if line[level] != ' ' {
        return 0, "", false
    }
    return level, line[level+1:], true
}
```
For level 7, Render uses line, not text. If line has emphasis tags, okay. If line is `####### ` trailing space, output includes trailing space. Original maybe. Fine.

