The skeleton needs a full implementation of the `List` class. The changes below implement all required operations using manual loops and index assignment, avoiding `Array.prototype` methods.

- `constructor` stores a copied list of items.
- `append` returns a new list containing this list followed by the other list.
- `concat` supports both no-argument flattening of the current list and argument-based concatenation by flattening the provided list one level and appending it to the current list.
- `filter`, `map`, `length`, `foldl`, `foldr`, and `reverse` are implemented without built-in array methods.

